    "description": "Took over support and ongoing development of BEPS, EarnUp's core transaction processing system (VB.NET, Microsoft SQL Server, IIS, Windows Server), supporting bill payments for approximately 3,000 customers.\n\nPart of the engineering team that migrated 130,000 customers into EarnUp's systems following the company's purchase of the PayMap service from Western Union; scaled the existing platform for the increased load by identifying performance bottlenecks and rewriting and optimizing code.\n\nIntegrated new banking partners for transaction processing over multiple years; extended platform functionality with services built in Python, Flask, and SQLAlchemy on PostgreSQL alongside the existing SQL Server database.\n\nBuilt and repeatedly re-architected a service integrating Jack Henry & Associates' iPay platform to process electronic payments, scaling to support up to 10,000 customers at peak as requirements changed.\n\nSupported daily transaction operations, including a manual morning validation and job-running process; automated the validation checks for daily ACH payment operations, reducing a process that took up to an hour and multiple staff to under five minutes with no human intervention.",
